# UI change verification

When editing dashboard HTML/CSS/HTMX or `:frontend-js` charts/DOM:

## Before calling done

1. **Viewport** — Judge layout at **laptop ~1280–1440px**, not only mobile. Cropped screenshots are not “mobile” unless the user says so.
2. **Cache** — Stylesheet must stay cache-busted (`/static/style.css?v=…`). New controls that look like native white buttons usually mean stale CSS.
3. **Interactions** — Prefer running `.agents/skills/ui-manual-qa` (or its STYLE/REGRESSION/HIST-ZOOM cases) after meaningful UI work; don’t rely on unit tests alone for click/zoom/view presets/scrubber pan.
4. **Visuals** — If appearance changed for README/User Guide, run docs-screenshot-refresh when shipping docs.
5. **Safety chrome** — Keep Simulation / Dry Run obvious; never hide trading-mode clarity.

## Common misses (regression smells)

- Squished LIVE + Data Age header cluster
- Concatenated deviation legend (“Over targetUnder target”)
- History Views/Zoom unstyled native buttons
- View presets that don’t hide series (Day · Total only)
- Chart drag that both zooms and pans without a separate pan control
- Scrubber stays disabled after drag/wheel zoom (only toolbar Zoom synced it)
- Scrubber thumb moves but chart does not pan (`options.scales` write ignored — need `chart.zoomScale`)
